        "id": "EX-CORE-WU04-skill-K-SOUND-repair-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Sound foundation: repair",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "When you missed the words, use the taught whole repetition-request chunk and pause for the other person. If the word is unknown, repetition alone may not help: point to the unclear part or ask for meaning using language you already know. The request chunk does not introduce all of its internal grammar.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "请再说一遍",
                "pinyin": "qǐngzàishuōyībiàn",
                "meaning": "please say it once more",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "d067378704cc216bbf96aa487b12844cc687e51a9f702cca94f1f73fa0921d5e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Your partner spoke while you were distracted; you did not hear the message. Its content is unspecified. Ask for repetition with the taught chunk, wait, then acknowledge hearing the repeated turn without inventing its content.\nFamiliar meanings available: please say it once more."
          }
        ]
      },
